shing work — if they are, the wall-clock savings would be direct; if they're on different streams, there might be less benefit due to overlapping execution. I need to look at the actual Trace Commit implementation to understand the execution flow and confirm this would actually help.\n\nNow I'm diving into the source code to examine the Trace Commit flow, see where zero hashes are calculated and whether they can be precomputed, check if MLE Rounds evaluations can be parallelized across streams, and identify any other quick optimizations I might have overlooked.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4218,"cache_read_input_tokens":65342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4218},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3","uuid":"59fc625b-402e-44e5-9211-c15091a73d84"}
