{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a99410f790eedc203","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhnvK56nsQ6TjyPt7YHv8M","description":"Research GKR round structure","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"I'm optimizing a GPU prover's STARK proof time. I need to understand the GKR (Grand Product Check / LogUp) rounds to identify optimization opportunities.\n\nSearch in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/` for:\n1. The GKR round implementation - the sumcheck rounds of the GKR protocol\n2. How the `fractional_sumcheck_gkr` module works - what operations happen per round\n3. Whether there are any per-AIR operations within GKR rounds that could be batched\n4. The relationship between GKR input evaluation and GKR rounds\n\nKey patterns to search for:\n- `fractional_sumcheck_gkr`\n- `compute_round_and_revert`\n- `multifold_kernel`\n- `precompute_m_build_partial`\n- `bit_rev_frac_build_k2`\n- `gkr` in filenames\n\nFocus on:\n- Is the GKR protocol operating on a single combined polynomial (all AIRs combined) or per-AIR?\n- What are the sequential dependencies between GKR rounds?\n- Where is the most time spent within each GKR round?\n\nRead the key files and report concisely with file paths and line numbers.","uuid":"af9a696e-91d6-43de-9e02-dedf0462df96","session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SfDXbvhPCSJscqwvCq5qYC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! ## Async frees and peak memory\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Many logup/zerocheck GPU helpers allocate temporary device buffers and launch kernels. Those\n4\t//! buffers are freed via cudaFreeAsync through the VPMM pool, so frees are only stream-ordered. If\n5\t//! new allocations happen before the current stream is synchronized, physical peak memory can\n6\t//! temporarily include both the old and new buffers even though MemTracker only sees the logical\n7\t//! max. Callers that care about physical peak should ensure a current-stream sync after use (e.g.\n8\t//! by calling `to_host()` on outputs or `current_stream_sync()`).\n9\t\n10\tuse std::{\n11\t    cmp::max,\n12\t    collections::hash_map::Entry,\n13\t    iter::{self, zip},\n14\t    sync::Arc,\n15\t};\n16\t\n17\tuse itertools::{izip, Itertools};\n18\tuse openvm_cuda_common::{\n19\t    copy::{MemCopyD2H, MemCopyD2HStreamSync, MemCopyH2D},\n20\t    d_buffer::DeviceBuffer,\n21\t    error::MemCopyError,\n22\t    memory_manager::MemTracker,\n23\t    stream::current_stream_sync,\n24\t};\n25\tuse openvm_stark_backend::{\n26\t    air_builders::symbolic::SymbolicConstraints,\n27\t    calculate_n_logup,\n28\t    dft::Radix2BowersSerial,\n29\t    p3_matrix::dense::RowMajorMatrix,\n30\t    poly_common::{\n31\t        eq_uni_poly, eval_eq_mle, eval_eq_sharp_uni, eval_eq_uni, eval_eq_uni_at_one,\n32\t        UnivariatePoly,\n33\t    },\n34\t    proof::{column_openings_by_rot, BatchConstraintProof, GkrProof},\n35\t    prover::{\n36\t        fractional_sumcheck_gkr::Frac, poly::eq_sharp_uni_poly, stacked_pcs::StackedLayout,\n37\t        sumcheck::sumcheck_round0_deg, ColMajorMatrix, CommittedTraceData,\n38\t        DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey, DeviceStarkProvingKey, MatrixDimensions, ProvingContext,\n39\t    },\n40\t};\n41\tuse p3_dft::TwoAdicSubgroupDft;\n42\tuse p3_field::{Field, PrimeCharacteristicRing, TwoAdicField};\n43\tuse p3_util::{log2_ceil_usize, log2_strict_usize};\n44\tuse rustc_hash::FxHashMap;\n45\tuse tracing::{debug, info, info_span, instrument};\n46\t\n47\tuse crate::{\n48\t    base::DeviceMatrix,\n49\t    cuda::{\n50\t        logup_zerocheck::{\n51\t            batched_interpolate_columns_gpu, fold_selectors_round0, InterpColDesc, MainMatrixPtrs,\n52\t        },\n53\t        sumcheck::batch_fold_mle,\n54\t    },\n55\t    data_transporter::transport_matrix_d2h_col_major,\n56\t    error::LogupZerocheckError,\n57\t    gpu_backend::GenericGpuBackend,\n58\t    hash_scheme::GpuHashScheme,\n59\t    cuda::logup_zerocheck::{\n60\t        _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n61\t        _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n62\t    },\n63\t    logup_zerocheck::{\n64\t        batch_mle::evaluate_zerocheck_batched, fold_ple::fold_ple_evals_rotate,\n65\t        gkr_input::TraceInteractionMeta, round0::evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu,\n66\t    },\n67\t    poly::EqEvalLayers,\n68\t    prelude::{EF, F},\n69\t    sponge::GpuFiatShamirTranscript,\n70\t    utils::compute_barycentric_inv_lagrange_denoms,\n71\t};\n72\t\n73\tpub(crate) mod batch_mle;\n74\tpub(crate) mod batch_mle_monomial;\n75\tmod errors;\n76\tpub(crate) mod fold_ple;\n77\t/// Fraction sumcheck via GKR\n78\tmod fractional;\n79\t/// Logup interaction evaluations for GKR input\n80\tmod gkr_input;\n81\tmod mle_round;\n82\tmod round0;\n83\tpub(crate) mod rules;\n84\t\n85\tuse batch_mle::{evaluate_logup_batched, TraceCtx};\n86\tuse batch_mle_monomial::{\n87\t    compute_lambda_combinations, compute_logup_combinations, get_num_monomials,\n88\t    get_zerocheck_rules_len, trace_has_monomials, LogupCombinations, LogupMonomialBatch,\n89\t    ZerocheckMonomialBatch, ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch,\n90\t};\n91\tpub use errors::*;\n92\tpub use fractional::{fractional_sumcheck_gpu, make_synthetic_leaves};\n93\tuse gkr_input::{collect_trace_interactions, log_gkr_input_evals};\n94\tuse round0::evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu;\n95\t\n96\t/// Number of OS threads (and thus CUDA streams) for parallel Round 0 processing.\n97\t/// More threads = more concurrent kernels but more peak GPU memory and more\n98\t/// MemoryManager mutex contention. 8 provides good SM utilization on the RTX 4090.\n99\tconst NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS: usize = 8;\n100\t\n101\t/// When `num_monomials >= DAG_FALLBACK_MONOMIAL_RATIO * rules_len`, use DAG evaluation\n102\t/// instead of the monomial kernel for high num_y traces.\n103\t/// This ratio can be tuned. Currently it is set to prefer the monomial kernel except for the\n104\t/// Poseidon2Air where the DAG node size is much smaller than number of monomials.\n105\tconst DAG_FALLBACK_MONOMIAL_RATIO: usize = 2;\n106\t\n107\t#[inline]\n108\tpub(crate) fn air_width_for_mat(need_rot: bool, mat_width: usize) -> u32 {\n109\t    if need_rot {\n110\t        debug_assert_eq!(mat_width % 2, 0, \"rotated matrices should have even width\");\n111\t        (mat_width / 2) as u32\n112\t    } else {\n113\t        mat_width as u32\n114\t    }\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t/// Result of processing one AIR in Round 0.\n118\tstruct Round0AirResult {\n119\t    trace_idx: usize,\n120\t    zerocheck_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n121\t    logup_numer_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n122\t    logup_denom_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n123\t}\n124\t\n125\t/// All read-only references needed to process one AIR in Round 0.\n126\tstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n127\t    trace_idx: usize,\n128\t    single_pk: &'a DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n129\t    n: isize,\n130\t    selectors_cube: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n131\t    public_values: &'a DeviceBuffer<F>,\n132\t    eq_3bs: &'a [EF],\n133\t    cached_mains: &'a [CommittedTraceData<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>],\n134\t    common_main: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n135\t    eq_xis: &'a FxHashMap<usize, EqEvalLayers<EF>>,\n136\t    d_lambda_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n137\t    beta_pows: &'a [EF],\n138\t    l_skip: usize,\n139\t    constraint_degree: usize,\n140\t    xi: &'a [EF],\n141\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n142\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates buffer capacity needed\n143\t    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n144\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums buffer capacity needed\n145\t    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n146\t    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates buffer capacity needed\n147\t    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n148\t    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums buffer capacity needed\n149\t    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n150\t}\n151\t\n152\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n153\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n154\t    bufs: &mut round0::Round0ThreadBuffers,\n155\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n156\t    let single_pk = w.single_pk;\n157\t    let single_air_constraints = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n158\t    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n159\t    assert!(\n160\t        local_constraint_deg <= w.constraint_degree,\n161\t        \"Max constraint degree ({local_constraint_deg}) of AIR exceeds the global maximum {}\",\n162\t        w.constraint_degree\n163\t    );\n164\t\n165\t    let log_large_domain = log2_ceil_usize(local_constraint_deg << w.l_skip);\n166\t    let omega_root = F::two_adic_generator(log_large_domain);\n167\t    assert!(!w.xi.is_empty(), \"xi vector must not be empty\");\n168\t\n169\t    let height = w.common_main.height();\n170\t    let mut main_parts = Vec::with_capacity(w.cached_mains.len() + 1);\n171\t    for committed in w.cached_mains {\n172\t        main_parts.push(committed.trace.buffer().as_ptr());\n173\t    }\n174\t    main_parts.push(w.common_main.buffer().as_ptr());\n175\t    let d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()?;\n176\t\n177\t    let n_lift = w.n.max(0) as usize;\n178\t    let eq_xi_tree = &w.eq_xis[&n_lift];\n179\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n180\t\n181\t    // Check if pre-allocated zerocheck buffers are large enough for this AIR\n182\t    let zc_prealloc_inter = if w.zc_intermed_cap > 0\n183\t        && bufs.zc_intermediates.len() >= w.zc_intermed_cap\n184\t    {\n185\t        Some(&mut bufs.zc_intermediates)\n186\t    } else {\n187\t        None\n188\t    };\n189\t    let zc_prealloc_temp = if w.zc_temp_sums_cap > 0\n190\t        && bufs.zc_temp_sums.len() >= w.zc_temp_sums_cap\n191\t    {\n192\t        Some(&mut bufs.zc_temp_sums)\n193\t    } else {\n194\t        None\n195\t    };\n196\t\n197\t    let sum_buffer = evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(\n198\t        single_pk,\n199\t        w.selectors_cube.buffer(),\n200\t        &d_main_parts,\n201\t        w.public_values,\n202\t        eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n203\t        w.d_lambda_pows,\n204\t        1 << w.l_skip,\n205\t        1 << n_lift,\n206\t        height as u32,\n207\t        num_cosets_zc as u32,\n208\t        omega_root,\n209\t        w.max_temp_bytes,\n210\t        zc_prealloc_inter,\n211\t        zc_prealloc_temp,\n212\t    )?;\n213\t\n214\t    let zerocheck_poly = if !sum_buffer.is_empty() {\n215\t        let q_evals = sum_buffer.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n216\t        let q = {\n217\t            let mut values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_zc << w.l_skip);\n218\t            for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_zc {\n219\t                for i in 0..1 << w.l_skip {\n220\t                    values[i * num_cosets_zc + coset_idx] = q_evals[(coset_idx << w.l_skip) + i];\n221\t                }\n222\t            }\n223\t            UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n224\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(values, num_cosets_zc),\n225\t                omega_root,\n226\t                omega_root,\n227\t            )\n228\t        };\n229\t        let sp_0_deg = sumcheck_round0_deg(w.l_skip, local_constraint_deg);\n230\t        let coeffs = (0..=sp_0_deg)\n231\t            .map(|i| {\n232\t                let mut c = -*q.coeffs().get(i).unwrap_or(&EF::ZERO);\n233\t                if i >= 1 << w.l_skip {\n234\t                    c += q.coeffs()[i - (1 << w.l_skip)];\n235\t                }\n236\t                c\n237\t            })\n238\t            .collect_vec();\n239\t        Some(UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs))\n240\t    } else {\n241\t        None\n242\t    };\n243\t\n244\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n245\t\n246\t    // Check if pre-allocated logup buffers are large enough for this AIR\n247\t    let logup_prealloc_inter = if w.logup_intermed_cap > 0\n248\t        && bufs.logup_intermediates.len() >= w.logup_intermed_cap\n249\t    {\n250\t        Some(&mut bufs.logup_intermediates)\n251\t    } else {\n252\t        None\n253\t    };\n254\t    let logup_prealloc_temp = if w.logup_temp_sums_cap > 0\n255\t        && bufs.logup_temp_sums.len() >= w.logup_temp_sums_cap\n256\t    {\n257\t        Some(&mut bufs.logup_temp_sums)\n258\t    } else {\n259\t        None\n260\t    };\n261\t\n262\t    let sum = evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(\n263\t        single_pk,\n264\t        &single_air_constraints,\n265\t        w.selectors_cube.buffer(),\n266\t        &d_main_parts,\n267\t        w.public_values,\n268\t        eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n269\t        w.beta_pows,\n270\t        w.eq_3bs,\n271\t        1 << w.l_skip,\n272\t        1 << n_lift,\n273\t        height as u32,\n274\t        num_cosets_logup as u32,\n275\t        omega_root,\n276\t        w.max_temp_bytes,\n277\t        logup_prealloc_inter,\n278\t        logup_prealloc_temp,\n279\t    )?;\n280\t\n281\t    let (logup_numer_poly, logup_denom_poly) = if !sum.is_empty() {\n282\t        let evals = sum.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n283\t        let (mut numer, denom): (Vec<EF>, Vec<EF>) =\n284\t            evals.into_iter().map(|frac| (frac.p, frac.q)).unzip();\n285\t        if w.n.is_negative() {\n286\t            let norm_factor = F::from_u32(1 << w.n.unsigned_abs()).inverse();\n287\t            for s in &mut numer {\n288\t                *s *= norm_factor;\n289\t            }\n290\t        }\n291\t        let mut numer_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << w.l_skip);\n292\t        let mut denom_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << w.l_skip);\n293\t        for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_logup {\n294\t            for i in 0..1 << w.l_skip {\n295\t                let src = (coset_idx << w.l_skip) + i;\n296\t                let dst = i * num_cosets_logup + coset_idx;\n297\t                numer_values[dst] = numer[src];\n298\t                denom_values[dst] = denom[src];\n299\t            }\n300\t        }"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01P1z3tfjrVZYw9WTeorpZw8","session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3","uuid":"14be63cb-4224-4893-b52e-07311d1fb4a0","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:50:55.303Z"}
